  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "On a particular Saturday, the prices of houses sold in Geelong, Victoria, ranged from $\\$294\\,000$ to $\\$618\\,000$. Show how to group the selling prices of the houses into eight classes.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "One suitable grouping, in dollars, is: $250\\,000$–$299\\,999$; $300\\,000$–$349\\,999$; $350\\,000$–$399\\,999$; $400\\,000$–$449\\,999$; $450\\,000$–$499\\,999$; $500\\,000$–$549\\,999$; $550\\,000$–$599\\,999$; $600\\,000$–$649\\,999$.",
      "worked": "Choose a convenient class width of $\\$50\\,000$ and start at $\\$250\\,000$. Eight consecutive classes then cover both the lowest price, $\\$294\\,000$, and the highest price, $\\$618\\,000$.\n\nThe class intervals, in dollars, are:\n\n$250\\,000$–$299\\,999$;\n$300\\,000$–$349\\,999$;\n$350\\,000$–$399\\,999$;\n$400\\,000$–$449\\,999$;\n$450\\,000$–$499\\,999$;\n$500\\,000$–$549\\,999$;\n$550\\,000$–$599\\,999$;\n$600\\,000$–$649\\,999$.",
